# SQL's `NOT` in capitals: DS0105 with a fix to `not`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where NOT isnull(amount)
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..45
  PIPELINE@0..44
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..44
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      PREFIX_EXPR@26..44
        IDENT@26..29 "NOT"
        WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
        CALL_EXPR@30..44
          NAME_REF@30..36
            IDENT@30..36 "isnull"
          ARG_LIST@36..44
            L_PAREN@36..37 "("
            NAME_REF@37..43
              IDENT@37..43 "amount"
            R_PAREN@43..44 ")"
  WHITESPACE@44..45 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `NOT` in capitals
  --> query:1:27
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where NOT isnull(amount)
  |                           ^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `not`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where not isnull(amount)
which parses without errors
